## SECTION 5 — AUDIENCE INTELLIGENCE
**who_they_are:** Existing or recent press-on wearers, mostly DIY-first, who have already had at least one set fail early (popped off within hours/days). Not total beginners — they know press-ons exist and have tried them, but are frustrated by inconsistent wear time.

**what_they_want_from_this_post:** A consolidated, no-fluff checklist that fixes the whole routine (prep → application → daily habits → removal) rather than one isolated tip. They want reassurance that failure is fixable, not inherent to the product.

**what_frustrates_them:** Generic advice repeated everywhere ("buff your nails") without addressing *why* their specific nail keeps failing (same finger, same water exposure, same timing pattern). Also frustrated by being told to just "buy better glue" when their prep was the real issue.

**top_5_pain_points:**
1. Nails pop off within hours or 1 day despite "following the guide"
2. Same one or two fingers (thumb/index) always fail first
3. Confusion over glue vs. adhesive tabs for longevity specifically
4. Uncertainty on how soon they can shower/wash dishes after applying
5. Fear that reapplying or troubleshooting will damage their natural nails

**exact_user_phrases:**
- "why do my press on nails keep falling off"
- "how do you keep your press-on nails on your nail without them snapping off"
- "how to make press-on nails stay on for a month"
- "lasted maybe a week, tops, before they started popping off"
- "I know it's possible" (re: 10-14 day wear)
- "my press-ons lasted me 3 weeks!!!"
- "if you push down in the middle of both the nails that it creates air bubbles"
- "90% of people complain that press-ons don't last"

**intent_content_signals:** Numbered, scannable tip format performs best (7-11 tips is the competitor norm); readers respond to cause-and-effect framing ("do X because Y happens"); concrete timeframes (30 seconds, 1-2 hours, 2 weeks) build trust; troubleshooting-table style content earns strong engagement (Hana Nail's structured approach).

